---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { GITHUB } from '../../lib/config.mjs';
import { loadPackages } from '../../lib/packages.mjs';
const packages = loadPackages();
const pick = ['org.oscairn.sampler', 'org.oscairn.effects', 'org.oscairn.step-sequencer', 'org.oscairn.fm-cartridges'];
const featured = pick.map((id) => packages.find((p) => p.id === id)).filter(Boolean);
---
<SiteLayout title="Oscairn" description="Oscairn is an open instrument platform: one realtime host for synthesis engines, samplers, effects and sequencers, made for stage keyboards and the desktop.">
<div class="hero"><div class="wrap grid">
<div><div class="tag"><span class="led"></span>Open instrument platform</div>
<h1>Oscairn</h1>
<p class="lead">Oscairn is an open instrument platform: one realtime host for synthesis engines, samplers, effects and sequencers, made for stage keyboards and the desktop.</p>
<div class="btns"><a class="btn p" href="/docs/">Read the docs</a><a class="btn s" href={GITHUB}>Get the source</a></div></div>
<div class="screen" aria-label="Placeholder for a screenshot"><div class="ph">PLACEHOLDER<br>Oscairn's own UI will be shown here.<br>No screenshot yet.</div></div>
</div></div>
<section><div class="wrap"><p class="lab">What it does</p><h2>Built for playing live</h2><div class="feat"><article class="card"><span class="n">01</span><h3>One engine, many sounds</h3><p>An engine with sound contexts holds several prepared sounds in one instance. Each MIDI channel picks one, and switching reloads nothing and keeps held notes playing.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="n">02</span><h3>Seamless Performance changes</h3><p>Open another Performance from a setlist or the library and the outgoing one's held notes and tails ring out while new notes play the new one.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="n">03</span><h3>Plugins in their own processes</h3><p>The desktop app runs plugins in isolated worker processes, with restarts and memory limits, so a plugin that fails stays out of the audio engine.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="n">04</span><h3>Your sounds are files</h3><p>Sounds and Performances are plain folders in a documented format. A library, or one Performance with its samples, exports to a single archive file.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section><div class="wrap fit"><div><p class="lab">How it fits together</p><h2>Audio on its own, everything else around it</h2>
<p>The UI never runs on the audio thread. It reaches the engine through a control API, so the same engine serves a keyboard's screen and a desktop window. Plugins run in worker processes, and new engines and effects arrive as signed packages.</p><p>The UI and the hardware panel talk to the engine; the engine runs plugins in isolated worker processes; signed packages install new engines and effects.</p></div>
<svg class="diagram" viewBox="0 0 560 500" role="img" aria-label="Diagram: UI and panel connect to the engine, the engine runs plugins in worker processes, packages install plugins" width="100%"><defs><marker id="ah" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z" fill="var(--line)"/></marker></defs><rect class="box" x="20" y="20" width="240" height="76" rx="6"/><text class="dt" x="140.0" y="54.0" text-anchor="middle">UI (Rust)</text><text class="ds" x="140.0" y="74.0" text-anchor="middle">touch, buttons, encoders</text><rect class="box" x="300" y="20" width="240" height="76" rx="6"/><text class="dt" x="420.0" y="54.0" text-anchor="middle">Keys, panel, audio</text><text class="ds" x="420.0" y="74.0" text-anchor="middle">the instrument or the desktop</text><line class="ln" x1="140" y1="96" x2="140" y2="160" marker-start="url(#ah)" marker-end="url(#ah)"/><text class="ds" x="150" y="134">control API</text><line class="ln" x1="420" y1="96" x2="420" y2="160" marker-start="url(#ah)" marker-end="url(#ah)"/><rect class="box hot" x="20" y="160" width="520" height="80" rx="6"/><text class="dt" x="280.0" y="196.0" text-anchor="middle">Engine</text><text class="ds" x="280.0" y="216.0" text-anchor="middle">realtime audio, sound contexts, Performances</text><rect class="grp" x="20" y="270" width="520" height="112" rx="8"/><text class="ds" x="32" y="290">isolated worker processes</text><rect class="box" x="34" y="300" width="156" height="66" rx="6"/><text class="dt" x="112.0" y="329.0" text-anchor="middle">Worker</text><text class="ds" x="112.0" y="349.0" text-anchor="middle">instrument plugin</text><rect class="box" x="204" y="300" width="156" height="66" rx="6"/><text class="dt" x="282.0" y="329.0" text-anchor="middle">Worker</text><text class="ds" x="282.0" y="349.0" text-anchor="middle">effect plugin</text><rect class="box" x="374" y="300" width="156" height="66" rx="6"/><text class="dt" x="452.0" y="329.0" text-anchor="middle">Worker</text><text class="ds" x="452.0" y="349.0" text-anchor="middle">another plugin</text><line class="ln" x1="280" y1="240" x2="280" y2="270" marker-start="url(#ah)" marker-end="url(#ah)"/><rect class="box" x="20" y="420" width="520" height="66" rx="6"/><text class="dt" x="280.0" y="449.0" text-anchor="middle">Package repository</text><text class="ds" x="280.0" y="469.0" text-anchor="middle">signed engines, effects and content</text><line class="ln" x1="280" y1="420" x2="280" y2="384" marker-end="url(#ah)"/><text class="ds" x="292" y="408">install, signatures checked</text></svg></div></section>
<section id="packages"><div class="wrap"><p class="lab">Packages</p><h2>Engines, effects and content from a signed repository</h2>
<p class="eg">Four of the {packages.length} packages in the repository now, from its records.</p><div class="feat">{featured.map((p) => <article class="card pk"><div class="t">{p.kind}</div><h3><a class="cardlink" href={`/packages/${p.id}/`}>{p.name}</a></h3><p class="clamp">{p.summary}</p><p class="pkmeta">{p.latest} &middot; {p.platforms.join(', ') || 'any platform'}</p></article>)}</div>
<p class="more"><a href="/packages/">All packages</a></p></div></section>
<section id="status"><div class="wrap"><p class="lab">Status</p><h2>Pre-release</h2><div class="status"><p style="margin:0">Oscairn is pre-release alpha software. Formats and interfaces still change, and there is no stable release. A desktop app runs today. On hardware, one stage keyboard has been tried so far, as a bundle that runs beside the unit's own system; installing it is at your own risk and the project gives no warranty. Parts of the design in the docs are not built yet, and the docs say which.</p></div></div></section>
</SiteLayout>
